––– comment –––
Columnar analyzers with exclude filters (found in the #5006 review).
10000 distinct ints give generic-packed blocks, so NOT IN with two values goes through the linear values analyzer.
10000 strings of one length give const-length blocks whose last subblock is partial; under a case-sensitive
collation the raw string analyzer is used, and threads=1 leaves no rowid boundary to clip rows past the end.
––– input –––
sql() { mysql -h0 -P9306 --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -e "$1"; }
––– output –––
––– block: ../base/start-searchd –––
––– input –––
{ echo "CREATE TABLE t (s STRING engine='columnar', n INT engine='columnar');"; for b in $(seq 0 9); do echo "INSERT INTO t VALUES $(for i in $(seq $((b*1000)) $((b*1000+999))); do printf "(%d,'v%04d',%d)," $((i+1)) $i $i; done | sed 's/,$//');"; done; echo "FLUSH RAMCHUNK t;"; } | mysql -h0 -P9306 && echo ready
––– output –––
ready
––– input –––
sql "SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(n) FROM t WHERE n NOT IN (1,2) /*+ ColumnarScan(n) */; SHOW META LIKE 'index';" | tr '\t' ' '
––– output –––
9998 49994997
index n:ColumnarScan (100%)
––– input –––
sql "SET collation_connection=binary; SELECT COUNT(*) FROM t WHERE s != 'v0001' OPTION threads=1 /*+ ColumnarScan(s) */; SHOW META LIKE 'index'; SELECT COUNT(*) FROM t WHERE s NOT IN ('v0001','v0002') OPTION threads=1 /*+ ColumnarScan(s) */;" | tr '\t' ' '
––– output –––
9999
index s:ColumnarScan (100%)
9998
––– input –––
sql "DROP TABLE t;"
––– output –––
––– comment –––
Issue #5047: when every row of a block passes (here a constant string, so a const block of its hash), the analyzer
filled the row ids of a subblock four at a time and restarted the last n%4 from the first one. Only the last subblock
of a chunk can be partial: 8197 rows leave 5. Intersected with the id analyzer the filter stopped after the first row
of that subblock (8193 instead of 8197); on its own it returned id 8193 twice and lost 8197. One INSERT keeps
rowid = id-1; chunks under 8192 rows get no analyzers.
––– input –––
{ echo "CREATE TABLE t2 (s STRING) engine='columnar';"; echo "INSERT INTO t2 (id,s) VALUES $(printf "(%d,'a')," $(seq 1 8197) | sed 's/,$//');"; echo "FLUSH RAMCHUNK t2;"; } | mysql -h0 -P9306 && echo ready
––– output –––
ready
––– input –––
sql "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM t2 WHERE s='a' AND id>0 OPTION threads=1 /*+ ColumnarScan(s,id) */; SHOW META LIKE 'index';" | tr '\t' ' '
––– output –––
8197
index id:ColumnarScan (100%), $s_HASH:ColumnarScan (100%)
––– input –––
sql "SELECT id FROM t2 WHERE s='a' AND id>0 ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 5 OPTION threads=1 /*+ NO_ColumnarScan(id) */; SHOW META LIKE 'index';" | tr '\t' ' ' | paste -sd' ' -
––– output –––
8197 8196 8195 8194 8193 index $s_HASH:ColumnarScan (100%)
––– input –––
sql "DROP TABLE t2;"
––– output –––
